 "details": {
  "title": "I Cover the Waterfront",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Frank Sinatra’s record in his key, E (F♯ for the trumpet), about 67 and free at the start and end, concert B3 to E5. It keeps the notes he sings where the page names them: G♯ held over B6, his long B over E major 7 and E6, B over B7 in the bridge, B and C♯ on the third climb, E over the C7 before home, the tag’s high D, D♯ and E, his held E over D6/9. Over the guitar’s C♯7 the tune’s F♯ becomes E♯. A short line opens over E6/9 and A minor 6, and it closes over C major 7, F major 7 and A minor 6 over E, A falling to G♯.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Johnny Green and Edward Heyman (1933)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, with Sinatra’s notes where the Fret Finder page names them, on that page’s chords"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "E major concert (F♯ for the trumpet), Sinatra’s key"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, verse (free), verse, bridge, verse, tag, coda"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (icw-guitar.mp3), 3:04"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The page numbers its three intro bars In1 to In3, so its bar 1 is bar 4 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
